<p>UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer faces a critical parliamentary test on April 20 after reports that Peter Mandelson was appointed Britain’s ambassador to the United States despite failing UK security vetting during the appointment process in late 2024. Starmer said he was &quot;absolutely furious&quot; and called it &quot;totally unacceptable&quot; that he and other ministers were not told about the failed vetting. His government says Foreign Office officials had the power to override the security recommendation without informing him. The fallout has grown into a broader test of Starmer’s leadership. Opposition parties are calling for his resignation, and some Labour lawmakers are questioning his judgment and how he runs government. Ministers have publicly backed him ahead of his House of Commons statement, but scrutiny is only building: the sacked top Foreign Office civil servant, Olly Robbins, is due to testify before a parliamentary committee on Tuesday.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/f2hB6aHvmXWur6155gcUSqdp74UtJwmFNuhmzbIO41QGL8V0pCR7ImdAlSxHLkCy_hyGYhl6htnEYh3YMlqLlnc1VmSzffCpEs0TQBmMuXC9' alt='UK PM Keir Starmer (right) has insisted that he and other ministers were not told Peter Mandelson (left) had failed the vetting process.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Official dismissal: Starmer sacked Foreign Office head Olly Robbins on Thursday, blaming officials for letting Mandelson’s appointment go ahead despite security advice against it.</li><li>Mandelson baggage: Critics say the Washington posting was especially risky because Mandelson’s past association with Jeffrey Epstein had already made him a contentious choice for envoy.</li><li>Backlash over blame: Politico reports that aides and officials, angered by Starmer’s habit of blaming institutions and firing subordinates, are now openly questioning his leadership.</li><li>Existing weakness: Dawn says the controversy has hit a prime minister who was already unpopular with much of the public and facing unease among Labour MPs.</li></ul><blockquote>Absolutely furious - Keir Starmer</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Keir Starmer and Downing Street: The prime minister’s team says the scandal reflects a breakdown in accountability inside the Foreign Office, arguing that ministers were left in the dark about a major problem. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993370/uk-pm-to-face-grilling-from-mps-today-over-mandelson-scandal'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Opposition parties: Rivals argue that either Starmer knew more than he has admitted, or the appointment system under his watch was so dysfunctional that he is still responsible for the failure. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/20/monday-briefing-how-is-it-possible-the-prime-minister-didnt-know-about-mandelsons-vetting-failure'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Former civil servants: Ex-officials say Olly Robbins is being made the fall guy for a broader political failure, and warn that firing him before parliamentary scrutiny risks looking like scapegoating. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993370/uk-pm-to-face-grilling-from-mps-today-over-mandelson-scandal'>Dawn</a>, <a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e5369e6b-b5d7-4e04-9c43-4adb6d8c231e'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Labour insiders: Politico’s reporting says the Mandelson episode has merged with longer-running complaints that Starmer delegates too much, avoids confrontation, and then struggles to contain the fallout. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/keir-starmer-dangerous-leadership-style-uk-peter-mandelson/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3350654/allies-back-starmer-mandelsons-epstein-links-leave-uk-leader-fighting-his-job'>Allies back Starmer as Mandelson saga leaves UK leader fighting for his job</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/keir-starmer-dangerous-leadership-style-uk-peter-mandelson/'>Fatal flaw: Keir Starmer’s leadership vacuum threatens to swallow him up</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/20/monday-briefing-how-is-it-possible-the-prime-minister-didnt-know-about-mandelsons-vetting-failure'>Monday briefing: How is it possible the prime minister didn’t know about Mandelson’s vetting failure?</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/british-prime-minister-starmer-faces-angry-lawmakers-mandelsons-132195110'>British PM faces angry lawmakers over Mandelson&#x27;s appointment as ambassador</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993370/uk-pm-to-face-grilling-from-mps-today-over-mandelson-scandal'>UK PM to face grilling from MPs today over Mandelson scandal</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e5369e6b-b5d7-4e04-9c43-4adb6d8c231e'>Starmer battles for Downing Street future amid Mandelson vetting scandal</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/uks-starmer-faces-parliament-over-mandelson-vetting-as-resignation-demands-swirl'>British PM Starmer faces Parliament over Mandelson vetting as resignation demands swirl</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/04/19/drof-a19.html'>Starmer government facing collapse over Mandelson/Epstein scandal</a> - wsws.org</li></ul>